      dek: 'The Departmental Board approved four 25-year loans worth US$260 million. The opposition questioned financing over that term trucks and bins that will last less.',
      contexto: 'In 2026 Mario Bergara\'s administration asked Montevideo\'s Departmental Board to authorise off-budget financing through trust funds. The original request, according to Subrayado, was US$318 million over 25 years, across five lines: sanitation, cleaning, streets, sidewalks and a US$40 million Old City plan. The cleaning component contemplated, according to El Observador, buying 74 trucks, 254,000 in-home containers and 19,000 on-premises containers.',
